@baseUrl = https://localhost:7174
@token = PASTE_JWT_HERE
@academicYearId = 2
@courseId = 1
@branchId = 1
@semesterId = 2
@sectionId = 2

### 1) Automatic period setup (6 teaching periods + break + lunch)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/timetable-management/periods/automatic
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "academicYearId": 2,
  "startTime": "09:00",
  "endTime": "16:00",
  "periodDurationMinutes": 60,
  "workingDays": ["MONDAY", "TUESDAY", "WEDNESDAY", "THURSDAY", "FRIDAY"],
  "breaks": [
    { "type": "BREAK", "afterPeriod": 2, "durationMinutes": 15, "name": "Break" },
    { "type": "LUNCH", "afterPeriod": 4, "durationMinutes": 45, "name": "Lunch" }
  ]
}

### 2) Read periods
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/timetable-management/periods?academicYearId={{academicYearId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 3) Calendar + holiday setup
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/timetable-management/calendar
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "academicYearId": 2,
  "reviewed": true,
  "workingDays": ["MONDAY", "TUESDAY", "WEDNESDAY", "THURSDAY", "FRIDAY"],
  "holidays": [
    { "date": "2026-10-02", "type": "HOLIDAY", "description": "Approved holiday test" }
  ]
}

### 4) Read classrooms (migration seeds Room 101 from existing data)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/timetable-management/classrooms
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 5) Create a new Phase-5 draft for Section 2 / Semester 2
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/timetable-management/timetables
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "academicYearId": 2,
  "courseId": 1,
  "branchId": 1,
  "semesterId": 2,
  "sectionId": 2,
  "timetableName": "CSE Semester 2 Section B - Phase 5",
  "effectiveFrom": "2026-09-01",
  "effectiveTo": "2027-05-31"
}

# Copy the timetableId from the previous response.
@timetableId = 2

### 6) Get draft details
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/timetable-management/timetables/{{timetableId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 7) Weekly requirements (subjects 4 and 5 belong to CSE Semester 2 in supplied dump)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/timetable-management/timetables/{{timetableId}}/requirements
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "requirements": [
    { "subjectId": 4, "periodsPerWeek": 3, "blockSize": 1 },
    { "subjectId": 5, "periodsPerWeek": 3, "blockSize": 1 }
  ]
}

### 8) Get requirements + faculty options
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/timetable-management/timetables/{{timetableId}}/requirements
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### IMPORTANT prerequisite for generation
# The supplied dump has faculty_subject_allocations rows with subject_id NULL.
# Link an existing/current allocation to the required subject(s) using your existing
# faculty-subject-allocation API before expecting those subjects to auto-schedule.
# The generator will intentionally return NO_FACULTY_ALLOCATION otherwise.

### 9) Generate draft (structured unscheduled data is expected if faculty allocation is still missing)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/timetable-management/timetables/{{timetableId}}/generate
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "replaceGenerated": false
}

### 10) Generate missing only (never removes manual entries)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/timetable-management/timetables/{{timetableId}}/generate-missing
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "replaceGenerated": false
}

### 11) Validate draft
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/timetable-management/timetables/{{timetableId}}/validate
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 12) Publish - succeeds only when validation has no blocking conflict/unscheduled requirement
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/timetable-management/timetables/{{timetableId}}/publish
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 13) Published section view
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/timetable-management/views/section/2?academicYearId=2
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 14) Holiday occurrence check - weekly template remains; date occurrence is suppressed
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/timetable-management/occurrences?date=2026-10-02&sectionId=2
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
